 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by reading the ticket sequence value outside the lock in the `next()` method, allowing concurrent threads to read the same value and produce duplicates. The fix ensures the read-modify-write operation is fully enclosed within the lock, making the increment atomic and guaranteeing unique ticket numbers under concurrent requests.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/sequence.py b/tracker/sequence.py\nindex f76c315..c04e778 100644\n--- a/tracker/sequence.py\n+++ b/tracker/sequence.py\n@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ class TicketSequence:\n     def next(self):\n         with self._lock:\n             current = self._next\n-        self._store(current + 1)\n+            self._next = current + 1\n         self.issued.append(current)\n         return current\n \n",
